meta {
  name: 06 Poll for assignment invites
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/api/agent-listings/mine?page=0&size=20
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  page: 0
  size: 20
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{jwt}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body: isDefined
}

docs {
  Tuesday morning — I always check the platform first thing with my coffee to
  see if any owner has pinged me overnight.

  Persona doc references `GET /agent-assignments/mine` but the live spec only
  exposes `/agent-listings/mine`. Two different names for the same idea in
  the same product is going to confuse owners and agents both. (FINDING:
  naming inconsistency between `/listings/{id}/agent-assignment` POST and
  the agent-side `/agent-listings/mine` GET.)

  Expected: 200 with an empty page (no owner has invited me yet in this
  isolated run — that's a cross-persona dependency, not a bug).
}
